{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 23, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the morning sun surprisingly vibrant. He sat up in bed, a strange disconnect settling in his stomach. The floral wallpaper, the slightly lopsided nightstand, the way the light caught the dust motes dancing in the air – it was all *too* perfect, too…rendered. He reached out to touch the nightstand, and his fingers passed right through it. A jolt of pure, unadulterated panic shot through him. He looked down at his hands, noticing the unnaturally smooth skin, the perfect, symmetrical nails. A HUD materialized in his vision: Health: 100%, Stamina: 100%, Quest Log: Empty. He was in a video game. A very realistic, disturbingly immersive video game. He stumbled out of bed, his legs feeling strangely weightless, and looked around his bedroom with newfound, terrified awareness.\n\n***\n\nHe cautiously opened the door, revealing a perfectly manicured suburban street. The houses were identical, the lawns impossibly green, and a cheerful little gnome sat guarding Mrs. Henderson's rose bushes. A notification popped up on his HUD: \"Tutorial Complete: Welcome to Meadowbrook! Objective: Explore the area and familiarize yourself with the environment.\" Arthur groaned. This wasn't some grand adventure; it was a fetch quest disguised as reality. He felt a wave of despair wash over him. Was this his life now? A pre-programmed existence, dictated by lines of code and the whims of some unseen game master? He took a deep breath, trying to process the sheer absurdity of it all. He had to find a way out, had to break free from this digital prison, but where did one even begin to fight a game?\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.18361379206180573}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.48426344990730286}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.00023135847004596144}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.08630053699016571}, {"token": "▁morning", "logprob": -1.04504609